# Static host URL rules (Render Static / Netlify-style).
# Known prerendered routes MUST rewrite to their index.html BEFORE the SPA fallback.
# On Render Dashboard → Redirects/Rewrites mirror these rules when possible.
# Build also emits sibling `news.html` (etc.) so clean URLs work even when the
# SPA `/*` rewrite would otherwise serve the home shell for extensionless paths.
# Critical: /* → /index.html must be Action Rewrite (200), NEVER Redirect (301).
# A Redirect to /index.html breaks /terms /privacy /CV (clean URLs become /index.html).

# Prerendered pages (no trailing slash)
/about    /about/index.html    200
/terms    /terms/index.html    200
/privacy  /privacy/index.html  200
/news     /news/index.html     200
/account  /account/index.html  200
/gis-signin  /gis-signin/index.html  200
/CV       /CV/index.html       200

# CV canonical without trailing slash
/CV/  /CV  301

# Feed aliases → live API (same 4h cache as GET /v1/news)
/feed     https://api.interchouette.net/v1/news/rss.xml   301
/rss.xml  https://api.interchouette.net/v1/news/rss.xml   301
/atom.xml https://api.interchouette.net/v1/news/atom.xml  301

# SPA fallback: unknown paths → Angular shell (client ** → home)
/*  /index.html  200
